* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call !tkconfirm(sentence, lines, typed, res, msg, boxtitle, btns)       ALWAYS SEVEN ARGUMENTS: a call with fewer stops with "Argument count mismatch" (pad with '')
*
*   As $tk_confirm: the sentence wrapped at spaces and never altered, the explanation under it, a name to type when typed is not null, res 'run', 'cancel' or 'wrong'.
*   THE DEFAULT BUTTON IS CANCEL.  It runs nothing and changes nothing: the program runs its own command when res is 'run'.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine tkconfirm(sentence, lines, typed, res, msg, boxtitle, btns)
$catalog !tkconfirm

   call $tk_confirm(sentence, lines, typed, res, msg, boxtitle, btns)
   return
end

* END-CODE
